Cut remuxed HLS segments where the playlist says.

jellyfin/jellyfin#18383 (head 39bdf800d550), backported to 10.11.11 on
top of the patches nixpkgs carries. It differs from the PR only where
10.11 does: master's EscapeProcessArgument() is 10.11's
EncodingUtils.NormalizePath(), and the class carries one attribute
fewer. The PR's tests are left out, since nixpkgs does not run them.

Jellyfin builds a remux playlist from the file's keyframes on a grid
counted from 0:00, while ffmpeg's hls muxer counts its cuts from where
it started. After a resume the two drift apart, segment N holds later
video than the playlist says, and the Projector Roku stalls
(jellyfin/jellyfin#17966). The patch runs a remux of a file with
keyframe data through the segment muxer, with -segment_times taken from
the playlist.

Measured on DodgeBall (2026-10-31), replaying both rules over its 1,159
keyframes: the run resumed at 0:50 drifted from segment 57 on, up to
40 s ahead. Playlist segment 220 starts at 22:09.245, where the Roku
stopped, and the file named 220.ts started at 22:26.

